# Grounded 2025-10-10 alongside briefing-f34.gws; see focus/F35/notes.md and
# focus/F34/notes.md for the account and why it's uncertain which parts of it
# belong at 34 versus 35. Ceremony and ordinary time working differently are
# filed here as the "further out" half of the same gathering.
#
# No longer @provisional -- one account, not a settled description.

@segment     briefing-f35
@title       Focus 35 — The Gathering (upper)
@levels      F35
@duration    ~1m10s

say You are now in Focus 35.
pause 5
say Behind you, the gathering at Focus 34. Ahead, the clusters of Focus 42.
pause 6
say Whatever gathering is happening at 34 may be felt from further out here — the same event, seen with more distance.
pause 8
say Time and memory may not work quite the way they do at home. What's happening tends to matter more than what happened, or what's next.
pause 10
say If something like a ceremony, a briefing, or an exchange is underway, you don't need to catch every word — or any words at all — to receive it.
pause 10
say This place tends to respond to intention almost immediately. If something feels difficult, a change of thought is often enough to change it. Clear skies, and let the weather follow.
pause 10
say What's written here is drawn from one visit, not a settled description. Let your own account, if you keep one, stand beside it rather than under it.
pause 10
say Stay as long as feels right.
pause 8
